From: CHIP Builder <chip@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: RTL8723BS support (backport to 6.18)

The rtw88 directory from Luka Gejak's RTL8723B/RTL8723BS series -- branch
8723bs-v11 of https://github.com/MocLG/rtw, commit 183038a ("MAINTAINERS: add
entry for the RTL8723B rtw88 driver"), based on 7.2.0, under review on
linux-wireless and not yet merged -- dropped onto 6.18.48's rtw88, plus one
backport: 6.18's struct sdio_driver has no .shutdown member, so rtw8723bs.c
hooks shutdown through .drv.shutdown instead.

Only the RTL8723BS path is meant to build: the other rtw88 SDIO chips' 6.18
bindings don't match the newer shared sdio.c. Replaces the staging rtl8723bs
driver, which WPA2/WPA3 mixed-mode APs reject with status_code=1.
Firmware: rtw88/rtw8723b_fw.bin (v41, upstream linux-firmware).

diff -Nru a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/Kconfig b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/Kconfig	2026-08-28 01:22:54.000000000 -0500
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/Kconfig	2026-09-14 09:17:52.496965371 -0500
@@ -36,6 +36,10 @@
 	tristate
 	select RTW88_8723X
 
+config RTW88_8723B
+	tristate
+	select RTW88_8723X
+
 config RTW88_8723D
 	tristate
 	select RTW88_8723X
@@ -159,6 +163,20 @@
 
 	  If you choose to build a module, it'll be called rtw88_8723cs.
 
+config RTW88_8723BS
+	tristate "Realtek 8723BS SDIO wireless network adapter"
+	depends on MMC
+	select RTW88_CORE
+	select RTW88_SDIO
+	select RTW88_8723B
+	help
+	  Select this option to enable support for 8723BS chipset
+
+	  This module adds support for the 8723BS 802.11n SDIO
+	  wireless network adapter.
+
+	  If you choose to build a module, it'll be called rtw88_8723bs.
+
 config RTW88_8723DU
 	tristate "Realtek 8723DU USB wireless network adapter"
 	depends on USB
